  "question": {
    "text": "In a common emitter configuration with suitable bias, it is given than $\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{L}}$ is the load resistance and $R_{B E}$ is small signal dynamic resistance (input side). Then, voltage gain, current gain and power gain are given, respectively, by:\n[ $\\beta$ is current gain, $I_B, I_C, I_E$ are respectively base, collector and emitter currents]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8SOrZ",
      "text": "\n$\\beta \\frac{R_L}{R_{B E}}, \\frac{\\Delta I_E}{\\Delta I_B}, \\beta^2 \\frac{R_L}{R_{B E}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VFr6G",
      "text": "\n$\\beta^2 \\frac{R_L}{R_{B E}}, \\frac{\\Delta I_C}{\\Delta I_B}, \\beta \\frac{R_L}{R_{B E}}$\n",
